  "notes": "Miami/Atlanta dark riff-led minimalism. What separates this from the other single-riff entries on this bench is the size of the hole in the middle: the research says \"huge mid-range space\", so the motif is pushed to 78–100 — the highest melodic floor in this batch — over an 808 at 16–31, with nothing authored between them, and the drums drop out to expose the riff (`dropOutBeats` 0.8 over four beats). The riff itself is a chromatic neighbour figure, which is `halfStepDissonance` 0.32 with `intervals.step` 0.75: it moves by semitone around a centre and almost never leaps. The 808 is deliberately dominant, so it keeps heavy distortion, `slideProb` 0.7 and the hard glides. `timbreHint` is `horror_organ` for the dark bell/organ/string motif the paragraph names. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium and marks the internals [LOW-CONF]: credits and one profile, no production account. The inferred parameters are the kick and hat numbers and the melodic register bounds. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set — the research says the chord bed is sparse or absent — so chord variety comes from `chordDurationBeats` and three harmonic rhythms. The i–bII family at weight 2 is INFERRED from the chromatic-neighbour description and is the first thing to delete if this ever sounds more harmonic than the records.",
